<Layouts.public flash={@flash} current_user={@current_user} return_to={@return_to}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-8">
    <.header>
      Acceptable Use Policy
      <:subtitle>What you may and may not run on FluxVale.</:subtitle>
    </.header>

    <p class="text-xs text-ink-subtle">
      Last updated: November 9, 2026
      <%!-- set at the pre-merge push; the
      final push after sign-off re-verifies the date --%>
    </p>

    <%!-- #365: the AUP's text of record. Plain English, not gettext —
        this template is the policy's wording. The banned classes and the
        enforcement stance are the maintainer's decisions (Nov 3 2026).
        Advisory edits land here. --%>
    <.card class="space-y-4" data-testid="acceptable-use-policy">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">The short version</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        This policy is part of the Terms of Service. It applies to
        everything you run on FluxVale: every instance, every app. Run
        your own things. Don't use FluxVale to hurt people, networks, or
        the platform itself.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Not allowed on FluxVale</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-ink-muted">
        <li>Anything illegal under the laws that apply to you or to us.</li>
        <li>
          Cryptocurrency mining, including mining pools and token
          farming.
        </li>
        <li>
          Torrents, P2P file sharing, and warez: distributing unlicensed
          content.
        </li>
        <li>Bulk email, spamming, and unsolicited messaging.</li>
        <li>
          Scraping and bulk automated harvesting that burdens the
          platform or third parties.
        </li>
        <li>
          Malware: distributing malware, ransomware, botnets,
          or command-and-control infrastructure.
        </li>
        <li>
          Stress-testing tooling: DDoS and booter services, or
          load-testing systems you don't own or don't have permission to
          test.
        </li>
        <li>
          Circumventing platform limits or security, or interfering with
          other instances or the platform itself.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Enforcement</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        We can investigate suspected violations. We can suspend or terminate
        accounts and instances that break this policy.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        When an account is terminated for breaking this policy, wallet
        balance stays non-refundable. That is part of the refund policy's
        stance, and it applies here too.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Reports</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Seen something that breaks this policy? Tell us:
        admin@fluxvale.com
      </p>
    </.card>
  </div>
</Layouts.public>
